From 2e2817ca55556f81b67d62c0aeb21d6c9de0e3e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:08:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban move: refuse a machine: target with no
 host_reason naming state on it

t_01a1d95c41620e6c (acceptance 3 of t_01a1d3e177138cff, single queue). Over 24 h on the hub board
(2026-11-13T07:57Z..11-14T07:57Z) seven `moved` events set runs_on to one machine. Three carried no
host_reason and no target-side state: pickup-stall alarm moves through the operator call that pinned
published, portable work from one full machine to another (ev 1207880 worker-7 -> worker-1, ev 1210619
worker-7 -> worker-4, ev 1214908 worker-3 -> worker-8). Two of them stalled again on the new machine and
needed a second alarm move to pool:worker.

Why: kanban_move_pool required a host_reason only for a pin to a *pool* worker; any other machine:<x>
passed bare, and the pickup-stall alarm scope (kanban_pickup_stall_repin) explicitly allowed
["machine:<X>"] for "one other eligible machine" while the pool queue needed a free slot now. A capacity
stall is a condition on the source machine, not state on the target, so a new single-machine pin just
moves the stall.

Change:
- kanban_move_pool.check: every machine:<x> label needs a host_reason (host_reason_required); a host
  reason that only cites capacity (free slots, N/N, eligible now, full, idle) is refused
  (host_reason_capacity). The refusal points at runs_on ["pool:worker"] / `--pool`.
- Pickup-stall alarm scope (tool and operator-call route): a machine:<X> target needs the same
  host_reason; the pool queue no longer needs a free slot now (the card waits in the single queue);
  alarm how-to text recommends only the pool.
- Operator-call move accepts and forwards an optional host_reason; creator repin tool forwards it.
- Exceptions that carry target state keep working with a recorded default host_reason: the origin
  repin of a worker-first card and the stranded-label reroute.
- kanban_move / operator-call schema text and `--host-reason` help updated.

Tests: new tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_move_machine_target_guard.py (every machine target refused bare,
capacity-only refused, state reasons accepted, force does not waive); pickup-stall repin tests: alarm move
to machine:X without host_reason refused (tool and operator call, the 11-13 reason verbatim), the same
move to pool:worker accepted with no free slot, a host_reason move accepted. Existing move tests now pass
an explicit host_reason for machine targets.
